  "body": "Elevated to capture sweeping sea views, this distinctive character home combines original 1950s concrete construction with a thoughtful renovation for modern coastal living.\r\n\r\nTimber floors, wooden shutters and panelled ceilings bring warmth and personality, complemented by fresh, contemporary finishes throughout. It's a home that celebrates its character while making everyday living feel effortless.\r\n\r\nAt its heart, light-filled open-plan living flows through French doors onto a generous entertaining deck, where the ocean provides a spectacular backdrop. Morning coffee comes with a sea view, while long summer evenings invite you to gather with friends and enjoy the outlook.\r\n\r\nThe beautifully renovated kitchen complements the home's character and connects easily with the living and entertaining spaces, keeping you part of the conversation while the sea draws your attention beyond.\r\n\r\nWith approximately 160m² of floor area, four bedrooms and three bathrooms, there's space for the whole family to spread out. The master bedroom enjoys its own ensuite, while the downstairs bedroom and bathroom offer excellent flexibility for teenagers, guests or working from home. A Moisture Master ventilation system adds to everyday comfort, while the internal-access garage offers extra convenience.\r\n\r\nJust minutes from Waiake Beach and Browns Bay village, with zoning for Torbay School, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College, this is coastal living with the essentials close at hand.\r\n\r\nFEATURES YOU'LL LOVE:\r\n\r\n- Elevated position with sweeping sea views\r\n- Solid mid-century style concrete construction\r\n- Beautifully renovated, with original character retained\r\n- Four bedrooms and three modern bathrooms\r\n- Master bedroom with ensuite\r\n- Beautifully renovated kitchen\r\n- French doors opening to a generous sea-view entertaining deck\r\n- Flexible downstairs bedroom and bathroom\r\n- Moisture Master ventilation system\r\n- Approximately 160m² of floor area\r\n- Renovation works with CCC issued October 2026\r\n- Single internal-access garage, carport beneath the deck and additional off-street parking\r\n- Convenient to Waiake Beach, Browns Bay village and sought-after schools\r\n\r\nCharacter, contemporary comfort and a sea view that make coming home something special.\r\n\r\nWhy wait? Call NOW to make it yours!\r\n\r\nAUCTION: Thursday 19 November 2026 from 5pm at Ray White Milford (unless sold prior)  \r\nINFO: https://rwmairangibay.co.nz/MRG36120 (scroll down to documents)\r\n\r\nAll agent conjunctions welcome from day one.",
